  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Storm Glass",
    "overview": "The workbench is a calm purple-gray sky seen through glass. Rounded dark islands (project tree, editor, bottom panel) float on a slightly lighter violet frame that holds the title bar, tool rail and status bar. Nothing glows at rest. The single lilac accent is the lightning: it strikes only where attention must land right now (the active tool, a fuzzy-match letter, a focused field, the one primary action) and is gone everywhere else.\n\nThe mood is calm, dense, precise. This is a tool used for whole days, so chrome contrast stays low and information density stays high: 26px rows, 13px UI text, 22px code lines. Color carries meaning, not decoration; the warm syntax hues (coral keywords, ochre functions, periwinkle fields) are the brightest things on screen because the code is the work.\n\nEverything is native and drawn by iced in Rust: no web chrome, no gradients, no blur. Interactive surfaces are quiet until touched, answering hover with a faint white wash and press with a deeper one.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark tonal islands (10px corners) separated by a 5px gap of violet frame.",
      "One accent, Thunder Lilac, used surgically.",
      "Geist for interface, Geist Mono for code, both bundled.",
      "Flat panes; only floating surfaces cast shadows.",
      "Translucent interaction washes that work on every surface."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Lightning Rule",
        "body": "Thunder Lilac appears only where attention must land now. If two lilac things compete on one screen, one of them is wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wash Rule",
        "body": "Hover and press are translucent white washes (`hover-wash`, `pressed-wash`), never new solid colors, so one token reads on frame, island and popup alike.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Family Rule",
        "body": "Only Geist and Geist Mono. Hierarchy comes from weight (400/500/600) and the text-color ladder, not from size jumps; nothing in the workbench exceeds 14px.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Float-Only Shadow Rule",
        "body": "If it does not float over other content, it does not cast a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every color from the theme palette in `ui/theme.rs`; add a named constant before using a new shade twice.",
      "**Do** use `hover-wash` / `pressed-wash` for interaction feedback on any surface.",
      "**Do** keep UI text at 12\u201314px and let weight and the text ladder carry hierarchy.",
      "**Do** separate panes with tone and the 5px frame gap, not lines.",
      "**Do** use the in-house inline SVG icons, drawn in `muted` and lilac only when active."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use Thunder Lilac for decoration, large fills or more than one competing element per screen.",
      "**Don't** put shadows on panes, rows or anything that does not float.",
      "**Don't** introduce fonts beyond Geist and Geist Mono.",
      "**Don't** use web-style effects (gradients, blur, glow); the GUI is native iced.",
      "**Don't** make selection lilac; selection stays Selection Blue."
    ]
  }
}